compute $x$.

text:
To solve for \(x\) given the system of equations:

\[
\begin{align*}
3x + 4y - 12z &= 10, \quad \text{(1)} \\
-2x - 3y + 9z &= -4, \quad \text{(2)}
\end{align*}
\]

we will use the method of elimination. First, we will eliminate \(y\) by making the coefficients of \(y\) in both equations equal in magnitude but opposite in sign. We can achieve this by multiplying equation (1) by 3 and equation (2) by 4:

\[
\begin{align*}
3(3x + 4y - 12z) &= 3(10) \implies 9x + 12y - 36z = 30, \quad \text{(3)} \\
4(-2x - 3y + 9z) &= 4(-4) \implies -8x - 12y + 36z = -16. \quad \text{(4)}
\end{align*}
\]

Next, we add equations (3) and (4) to eliminate \(y\):

\[
(9x + 12y - 36z) + (-8x - 12y + 36z) = 30 + (-16) \implies 9x - 8x = 14 \implies x = 14.
\]

Thus, the value of \(x\) is \(\boxed{14}\).

